Example screens for screens_dir: copy this directory to /etc/bbs/screens
and set [general] screens_dir = /etc/bbs/screens.  The [menu main] in
bbs.conf.sample uses mainmenu and bulletins.

  NAME.ans    ANSI art, CP437      (ANSI terminals)
  NAME.asc    text with {tags}     (any text terminal; 3270s too)
  NAME.3270   text with {color}    (3270s)

Tags in a .asc ({clear}, {pause}, {red}, {on blue}, {bright}, {reset}...)
are ANSI on an ANSI terminal, colors on a Commodore and a 3270, and
nothing on a plain terminal: every .asc here has some, as do the sample
menus and strings in bbs.conf.sample.

logon, newuser, welcome and goodbye are shown by themselves; others by
the menus that name them.  See the wiki's Customization page.
